;; THE TEMPLATE THE KIT BRINGS WITH IT, as data. `bb init` generates an application from the
;; entry named by :default; the health-check report prints the same entry, so "these two were run
;; together" names exact commits on both sides.
;;
;; AN ENTRY IN DATA, NOT A CONSTANT IN CODE. The KIT ships one template. A second one - or an
;; adopter who brings their own application and wants none - must not need a code change: the
;; harness never looks inside a framework (it needs a git repository, gate commands and an nREPL
;; command in loop.edn, and Clojure source). Supported is not the same as possible: only the pair
;; the health check ran is certified.
;;
;; :git/sha is the PIN and is what resolves; :git/tag is a label for people. Bump both together,
;; and re-run the health check before committing the bump.
;;
;; DEVELOPING THE TEMPLATE: set KIT_TEMPLATE_LOCAL to a local clone's path and generation reads
;; that working tree instead of the pinned commit. Never for a published health-check record.
{:default :clojure-stack-lite
 :templates
 {:clojure-stack-lite
  {:template io.github.ontopro/clojure-stack-lite
   :git/url "https://github.com/ontopro/clojure-stack-lite.git"
   :git/sha "f6049dcc98c0cf8f536b8f69f26613360ae41c26"
   :git/tag "kit-v1.1"
   :as-of "2026-10-07"
   ;; upstream is abogoyavlensky/clojure-stack-lite (MIT); `git diff master..kit` in the fork is
   ;; everything the KIT changed. (`kit` there is a BRANCH; `kit-v1.1` a version of the template,
   ;; not of the KIT)
   :deps-new {:git/tag "v0.8.0" :git/sha "2f96530"}
   ;; WHAT A RUN AGAINST THIS TEMPLATE'S PROJECTS NEEDS TO BE TOLD, written by `bb init` into the
   ;; plan's `loop.edn` defaults. Three gates are tasks of the GENERATED `bb.edn`; the fourth, the
   ;; boundary gate, is the KIT's own, run against the project - `{{kit}}` becomes the KIT's
   ;; absolute path at `bb init`, because a gate runs in a worktree under work/ and no relative
   ;; path to the KIT holds from there. `:test` on the nREPL's classpath so a Tester can load
   ;; test namespaces; the generated `deps.edn` says why `:dev` is left out.
   :loop/defaults {:gates [[:fmt "bb fmt-check"] [:lint "bb lint"] [:test "bb test"]
                           [:deps "bb --config {{kit}}/harness/bb.edn boundary"]]
                   :nrepl/cmd ["clojure" "-Srepro" "-M:test:nrepl"]}
   ;; THE GENERATED APPLICATION'S LAYERS, written to its layers.edn by `bb init` and enforced by
   ;; the boundary gate above. Names are TAILS under the application's root namespace (`core` is
   ;; `xyx.core` in an application named xyx). This is the template's own require graph at the
   ;; pinned commit, declared rather than discovered: a namespace added later fails the gate until
   ;; it is declared - in the APPLICATION's layers.edn, which is its owner's to edit. core and db
   ;; stand alone (the system is wired by configuration, not by requires); views knows nothing;
   ;; handlers render views; routes name handlers; server composes both. test/ is not checked.
   :layers {core #{}
            db #{}
            views #{}
            handlers #{views}
            routes #{handlers}
            server #{handlers routes}}}}}
